description:
Objective: the host obtains exact pinned Linux claude and codex CLI binaries, for x64 and arm64, without trusting the network for their identity. A manifest pins each release file's URL and sha256. A controller-private cache downloads them, verifies them and serves them, like R03's image-cache.mjs for the Ubuntu image.

Split from CQ-R10d (task-90847011) on 2026-10-29. The human chose a host pinned cache plus a copy-only stream into the guest; the guest never downloads. It depends on CQ-R10d1 (task-9faf1ef3) only because both edit scripts/tests/local-runner-agents.test.mjs.

Contract:
- A new scripts/local-runner/agent-binaries.json, in the style of certified-provider.json:
  - schemaVersion 1;
  - for each cli (claude, codex, the CQ-R10b JOBS keys) and each arch (x64, arm64): {version, url, sha256, size};
  - when the release file is an archive, also the member path and the member's own sha256 and size.
  - The worker picks current stable releases, downloads them once, records their hashes and sizes, and documents the versions in the step note.
- A new scripts/local-runner/agent-cache.mjs:
  - a strict loader for the manifest's exact shape, accepting only fixed https URLs;
  - fetchAgentBinary({cli, arch, cacheDir, ...injectable download}), which resolves a verified {file, sha256, size} in a controller-private cacheDir;
  - a cache hit is re-verified, and a corrupt entry is removed and downloaded once more;
  - archive extraction, if any, is bounded and extracts only the pinned member;
  - fixed error codes, with no URL, path or body in a message;
  - image-cache.mjs's download and verify pattern is reused where it fits.
- Tests use a local HTTP fixture server or an injected download, never the network.

Out of scope: copying into the guest and readiness (CQ-R10d3), the argv and MCP config (CQ-R10d4), and any verified-local or isolation claim.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-agents.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs (on WSL: env -i with the nvm Node 24 PATH).

implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (red). Load test-driven-development.

scripts/tests/local-runner-agents.test.mjs is created by CQ-R10d1 (task-9faf1ef3); add rows to its LANDED bytes. Fixtures come from an INJECTED fetch, never the network: it returns {ok, status, url, headers, body: ReadableStream} per request, as the image-cache tests in scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs do. Test manifests use the real fixed URL templates with fixture sizes and hashes, and go through the same validator.

Rows (exact codes; each refusal also asserts that the cacheDir holds no file at all):
- AC1 loader (DoD 1): the shipped agent-binaries.json loads. validateAgentManifest refuses with AGENT_BINARY_MANIFEST_INVALID each of these:
  - a wrong schemaVersion, a missing or extra cli or arch, an extra key;
  - an http URL, or a URL other than its cli's fixed template;
  - a version that fails the strict pattern;
  - a non-64-hex sha256, or a size that is not a positive safe integer;
  - an archive entry missing member, memberSha256 or memberSize, or whose member is absolute, has '..', or has a backslash;
  - a manifest file over 64 KiB.
- AC2 download (DoD 2):
  - a matching body is kept at <cacheDir>/<sha256>.bin and returned as {file, sha256, size};
  - a wrong sha256 gives AGENT_BINARY_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH;
  - a declared or streamed size over the pin gives AGENT_BINARY_TOO_LARGE;
  - a redirect to http, a redirect chain over 5, or a non-2xx gives AGENT_BINARY_DOWNLOAD_FAILED;
  - a body that errors midway gives AGENT_BINARY_DOWNLOAD_FAILED.
- AC3 archive (DoD 2). A tar.gz built in-test (a few-line ustar writer with zlib.gzipSync) holding the member plus a decoy entry:
  - the member alone is extracted and verified;
  - a member whose bytes miss memberSha256 gives AGENT_BINARY_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH;
  - a missing member, a symlink or hard link at the member path, a corrupt header checksum or truncated gzip gives AGENT_BINARY_ARCHIVE_INVALID;
  - decompressed output past memberSize gives AGENT_BINARY_TOO_LARGE.
- AC4 cache (DoD 3):
  - a valid cached file makes zero fetch calls;
  - a cached file with one byte flipped is removed and downloaded exactly once more, then verified;
  - a cached directory or symlink is refused, and never followed or deleted;
  - two concurrent calls both resolve verified files, with no .part left.
- AC5: every error message is its fixed text and includes neither the URL, nor cacheDir, nor body bytes.

scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs: add 'agent-binaries.json' and 'agent-cache.mjs' to its `required` list, so the bundle provably ships them.

Run the verification command and confirm the rows fail for the missing module or manifest.

implementationPlan.note:
No byte change. scripts/local-runner/agent-cache.mjs (275 lines) is byte-equal to baa52df at HEAD b9ea011 and in the shared tree. I re-read it against the step-3 contract:
- validateAgentManifest (lines 59-74):
  - takes a structuredClone copy;
  - exact keys at every level, with schemaVersion 1;
  - strict VERSION, and url === the code-built URLS template;
  - 64-hex sha256, and a safe positive size ≤ 1 GiB;
  - codex also requires archive 'tar.gz', a plain relative member of ≤100 chars, memberSha256 and memberSize;
  - returns a deep-frozen copy.
- loadAgentManifest (76-82): the module-relative URL only, ≤64 KiB, then the same validator.
- fetchAgentBinary (265-275):
  - validates cli/arch/cacheDir/fetch before any I/O;
  - the manifest seam goes through validateAgentManifest;
  - mkdir uses 0700, and the target is <cacheDir>/<binary sha>.bin.
- respond (129-138): redirect 'manual', at most 5 hops, each Location resolved and required to be https, under AbortSignal.timeout.
- download (230-258):
  - the content-length and streamed bytes are bounded by pin.size into an exclusive 0600 .part with sync;
  - holdsPin verifies the archive before gunzip/untar;
  - the member is verified before rename;
  - every recorded .part is unlinked in finally.
- untar (176-216): header checksum; skips by size plus padding; only typeflag '0'/NUL at the member path, with no duplicate; size ≤ memberSize; decompressed total ≤ memberSize + 1 MiB; drains to EOF so the gzip trailer errors surface.
- Codes are AGENT_BINARY_* with fixed text, and refuse() maps any foreign code to a fixed one.
- Unchanged for QA: per the rejection, no code change and no re-slice.

